From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:59:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: samsung: acpm: add gs201 support

Google's ACPM driver for gs201 is the same source as for gs101: it finds
the firmware framework data at SRAM offset 0xa000 (initdata-base in
Google's gs201.dtsi), reads the AP channel count (ipc_ap_max) and the
channel table (ipc_channels) from it, and uses the same channel layout
and message format. Only the addresses differ: the AP2APM mailbox is at
0x18210000 and the APM SRAM at 0x18500000 (0x48000 bytes), which come
from the device tree.

Add the gs201 match data. Its clocks device is "gs201-acpm-clk", since
gs201 adds a paired GPU clock to the gs101 DVFS domains.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c b/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
index d2061f313..ea5b7c8bd 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/samsung/exynos-acpm.c
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #define ACPM_TX_TIMEOUT_US		500000
 
 #define ACPM_GS101_INITDATA_BASE	0xa000
+#define ACPM_GS201_INITDATA_BASE	0xa000
 
 /* Sanity limit for the channel count read from SRAM. */
 #define ACPM_MAX_CHANS			64
@@ -925,10 +926,18 @@ static const struct acpm_match_data acpm_gs101 = {
 	.acpm_clk_dev_name = "gs101-acpm-clk",
 };
 
+static const struct acpm_match_data acpm_gs201 = {
+	.initdata_base = ACPM_GS201_INITDATA_BASE,
+	.acpm_clk_dev_name = "gs201-acpm-clk",
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id acpm_match[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "google,gs101-acpm-ipc",
 		.data = &acpm_gs101,
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "google,gs201-acpm-ipc",
+		.data = &acpm_gs201,
 	},
 	{},
 };
